{"_v":1,"id":"fela-2009","cat":"broadway","cs":80.26,"rc":8,"bd":{"positive":7,"mixed":1,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Jennifer Farrar","o":"Associated Press","s":86,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.newstimes.com/entertainment/article/Review-Fela-dance-party-finds-its-way-to-B-way-262086.php","d":"2009-11-23","q":"\"Fela!\" is a unique Broadway experience that leaves the audience on their feet and wanting more."},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":83,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2009/legit/reviews/fela-3-1200477297/","d":"2009-11-23","q":"This blazingly energetic biographical musical about the Nigerian musician and activist Fela Kuti is a sensory assault of the most welcome kind, a show that fills the theater with pulsing Afrobeat rhythms and dazzling choreography."},{"cn":"David Cote","o":"Time Out New York","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/newyork/theater/fela","d":"2009-11-24","q":"Fela! is more than a musical; it's an ecstatic phenomenon."},{"cn":"Michael Billington","o":"The Guardian","s":79,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://www.guardian.co.uk/stage/2010/nov/17/fela-review","d":"2010-11-17","q":"The dancing is ecstatic, the music lifts the spirits, and the stage is alive with movement."},{"cn":"Elisabeth Vincentelli","o":"New York Post","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.nypost.com/p/entertainment/theater/plenty_of_afro_heat_kQGx3P1vFBYrLx0bbPQ1VK","d":"2009-09-24","q":"This is as close as Broadway gets to fully immersive theater."},{"cn":"Terry Teachout","o":"The Wall Street Journal","s":73,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10001424052748704013004574517680589230494?gaa_at=eafs&gaa_n=AWEtsqcIR5-MFpbAKxuP8PAAMZoRl3Sl8be4ZHxvfqui2FBekXnLQ_ncoCqd&gaa_ts=69a8fe76&gaa_sig=9on3xjumf1MPzqrP1ZUfKj8khD58FRxTQZSwon0_vrVkgJWAQElXqA-epYcn6WAHy9G9ugyexH9LEKMcoU2ylQ%3D%3D","d":"2009-11-25","q":"What saves 'Fela!' from being a mindless celebration is that it doesn'"},{"cn":"Elysa Gardner","o":"USA Today","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.usatoday.com/life/theater/reviews/2009-11-24-fela24_st_N.htm","d":"2009-11-23","q":"Fela! earns its exclamation point, joyfully and relentlessly."},{"cn":"Michael Sommers","o":"New Jersey Newsroom","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"https://www.newjerseynewsroom.com/movies/afrobeat-music-drives-broadways-new-fela","d":"2009-11-23","q":"Broadway has never before witnessed a musical quite like \"Fela!\" — an explosive mix of catchy Afrobeat rhythms, wild, sexy dancing and raw bio-dramatics — and while its unique charms certainly are powerful, one frankly wonders whether this unusual show will catch on with the mainstream public."}],"au":{"score":63,"designation":"Disliking","sources":{"mz":{"s":63,"c":26,"sr":3.2}}},"tn":[{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Choreography","n":"Bill T. Jones","w":true},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Costume Design of a Musical","n":"Marina Draghici","w":true},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Sound Design of a Musical","n":"Robert Kaplowitz","w":true},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Musical","n":null},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Book of a Musical","n":"Jim Lewis"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Book of a Musical","n":"Bill T. Jones"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Actor in a Musical","n":"Sahr Ngaujah"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Featured Actress in a Musical","n":"Lillias White"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Direction of a Musical","n":"Bill T. Jones"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Orchestrations","n":"Aaron Johnson"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Scenic Design of a Musical","n":"Marina Draghici"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Lighting Design of a Musical","n":"Robert Wierzel"}],"cn":{"t":"Critics praise this electrifying musical as an exuberant celebration, with Bill T. Jones's stirring choreography and pounding Afrobeat music creating an immersive, joyous theatrical experience that breaks down barriers between stage and audience.","rc":11},"bo":{"tw":null,"at":{"g":27110350,"p":416,"a":355451}},"ta":"230 W 49th St, New York, NY 10019","vs":{"sl":3,"so":4,"co":3,"am":4,"fa":3},"pd":"2009-10-19","ca":[{"n":"